# Line endings (audit 2026-10-29, T2).
#
# Without this file the repo relied on each machine's core.autocrlf. On a clone
# or a tool that doesn't set it, a file that Windows editors had flipped to CRLF
# showed up as a 2,900-line diff (cli-bridge.js, App.jsx), which hides the one
# real line that changed and makes review impossible.
#
# text=auto : git decides per file; text files are stored as LF in the repo and
#             compared as LF, so an editor flipping CRLF <-> LF is not a change.
#             Binary files (the case-study PDFs, images, the DB) are left alone.
# *.bat     : batch files must be CRLF on disk or cmd.exe can mis-parse labels.
* text=auto
*.bat text eol=crlf
